cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the accompanying paper."
title: "MESMER"
abstract: >-
  MESMER (Modular Earth System Model Emulator with spatially Resolved output) is
  a Python package for spatially resolved climate model emulation. It translates
  annual mean global climate trajectories into gridded fields of selected climate
  variables over land, accounting for both the forced local response and internal
  variability.
